        "text": "In fact, we only get the full picture much later and we can only determine markets and trends with certainty and hindsight. Lastly, you may have heard that the market moves in cycles with repeating trends. Almost every asset will experience cycles between bullish and bearish markets. Long term market cycles are more reliable than short term market trends and can be easily seen on graphs with decades of data. If you take a look at the stock market's performance or crypto markets over the past few years, you'll easily be able to identify the market cycle cycles. Shorter cycles will appear as you zoom in on shorter time periods. As with market trends, it's challenging to determine what stage of a cycle we're in and when a new one will begin. Understanding market trends and cycles is critical to be successful in trading and investing, but getting to know how market psychology impacts market trends is equally critical. We will learn what market psychology is in the next module.",
